         DIGITAL ANNOUNCES VICE PRESIDENT NETWORK PRODUCT
                   SALES AND MARKETING, EUROPE

 
GENEVA, Switzerland -- 12 December 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced the appointment of Guy Buyst to Vice 
President Network Product Sales and Marketing, Europe.  Mr. Buyst 
will be responsible for all sales, sales support, field marketing, 
and channels for Digital's Network Product Business in Europe.

     Formed in early 1994 as a segment of Digital's Components 
Division, the Network Product Business develops, manufactures, 
markets, and sells products worldwide to build open client/server 
networks.  It is one of the nine independent business units at 
Digital and is responsible for more than $550M in revenue and
significant profit in fiscal year 1994.  Products contributing to 
this revenue stream include hubs, routers, switches, network 
adapter cards, and emerging technologies for Ethernet over cable 
television.  

     "The Network Product Business is rapidly expanding into new 
markets and Europe is a key area of growth," said Jeffrey Low, 
worldwide Vice President of Sales and Marketing, Network Product 
Business at Digital. "Guy's extensive experience will be of great 
value toward building the European networking sales and marketing 
organization and distribution channels.  With our leading-edge 
product and channels strategy, Digital is well positioned to be
the market leader in the European networks industry."

     Mr. Buyst has held a series of executive positions with Anixter 
International, headquartered in Brussels.  His most recent position 
was as Director of Business Development for Europe during which time 
he was instrumental in implementing the distribution agreement with 
Digital.  Mr. Buyst studied as an industrial engineer in electricity 
and mechanics at the Katholieke Industriele Hogeschool in Antwerpen 
in 1977.  

     Digital, the leader in high-performance switched networking, 
continues to be a significant contributor to the development of 
many popular networking technologies including Ethernet, FDDI and 
ATM LANs, network switches, routers, bridges, network adapters, and 
terminal servers.  Digital has networked more than 10 million users 
worldwide.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software, and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
