            DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW TEAMLINKS OFFICE SERVER
               PACKAGE AND REDUCED PRICING FOR DEC VTX


MAYNARD, Mass. -- December 12, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the availability of a new TeamLinks Office Server 
package that reduces the price and simplifies ordering of the server 
components of Digital's TeamLinks Office suite of groupware 
applications.  In addition, Digital reduced the pricing of its DEC 
VTX electronic information distribution product by over 50%.

New TeamLinks Office Server Packages

     The new TeamLinks Office Server products include all the 
required server components in easy-to-order packages at a 40% 
savings over the cost if purchased separately. TeamLinks Office 
software is Digital's integrated suite of client/server groupware 
applications for Microsoft Windows and Macintosh users. It includes 
TeamLinks Mail (X.400 electronic mail), TeamLinks Routing 
(administrative workflow), TeamLinks Conferencing (conferencing/
bulletin board), DEC VTX (electronic information library), and 
Calendar Manager (group scheduling).  The TeamLinks Office Server 
packages may be ordered for electronic mail with either the ALL-IN-1 
Office Server or the MailWorks mail server. 

     Special upgrade packages are also available for existing TeamLinks 
Mail customers using ALL-IN-1 or MailWorks servers who want to take 
advantage of the capabilities of the entire TeamLinks Office 
applications suite.  The TeamLinks Office Server package with the 
ALL-IN-1 mail server is available for the OpenVMS operating system 
on both the Alpha and VAX platforms for $37,300 for new customers; 
the upgrade price is $16,200 for existing ALL-IN-1 customers. The 
TeamLinks Office Server package with the MailWorks mail server is 
available for the OpenVMS operating system on the VAX platform for 
$22,300 for new customers, the upgrade price is $20,200 for existing 
MailWorks customers.

New Reduced Pricing for DEC VTX Library Services

     Digital's price reduction of over 50% for the DEC VTX 
application enables departments and workgroups to take advantage of 
this electronic information distribution technology that has been 
typically used for enterprise wide solutions. DEC VTX is Digital's 
client/server electronic library application that supports the 
electronic distribution of information such as policies and 
procedures or product information to PC, Macintosh and VT terminal 
users. The DEC VTX database supports any data type such as text, 
graphics, image and video and includes a built-in content-based 
retrieval capability for faster access to information. DEC VTX is 
available as a standalone application or as part of the TeamLinks 
Office application suite.

     DEC VTX for OpenVMS software is available immediately with 
pricing starting at $5,000 for workgroup class systems, or only $249 
per Concurrent User license.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
