         InfoSoft to Port CONVEYOR Mainframe Conversion Tool
                To OpenVMS Platform on Alpha Systems


 ... Agreement includes availability worldwide, service, support ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- December 12, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and InfoSoft GmbH, of Dortmund, Germany, today announced an 
agreement under which InfoSoft's innovative CONVEYOR automatic 
mainframe application conversion tool will be ported to Digital's 
Alpha platform running the OpenVMS operating system. The agreement 
includes the implementation of product delivery programs by CONVEYOR 
service and support partners worldwide.

     CONVEYOR for OpenVMS systems will enable Digital to provide 
transparent migration of existing applications and data from 
mainframe systems to the Alpha environment. The mainframe 
environments covered include IBM MVS-VSE, CICS, and IMS, Bull GCOS7, 
Siemens Nixdorf BS2000, and Unisys OS1100. Of particular note are 
the IMS and CICS environments, which can now be migrated to the 
business-critical Alpha environment.

     CONVEYOR for OpenVMS systems will support popular relational 
databases, including Rdb, Oracle7, Ingres, and Sybase, as well as 
Digital products.

     "With the new partnership, we will be in a position to extend 
our presence considerably in the mainframe downsizing market." said 
Rolf Brandt, managing director of InfoSoft. "In our opinion, 
Digital's powerful Alpha environment represents an ideal target 
platform for the growing number of companies planning to move from 
mainframes to open systems."

     CONVEYOR will complement Digital's existing portfolio of 
mainframe downsizing solutions and make us even more competitive 
with a comprehensive range of mainframe downsizing tools, 
applications, and services," said Jesse Lipcon, Digital Vice 
President of OpenVMS Systems Business. "As Digital's mainframe 
downsizing opportunities increase, CONVEYOR will be a key to 
leveraging the competitive advantages of the OpenVMS platform in 
legacy environments from a number of mainframe vendors." 

InfoSoft CONVEYOR on Alpha Systems

     "As the company that first introduced many of the technologies 
to enable mainframe downsizing, Digital continues to introduce 
solutions that lead this market -- the highest performing 
semiconductors and systems, standards-based networking and operating 
environments, client-server software frameworks, as well as 
worldwide services and support," said Steve Koenig, Director of 
Digital's Mainframe Downsizing Program. 

     "The addition of CONVEYOR for the OpenVMS platform adds to our 
portfolio of leading migration tools available worldwide on the 
industry's leading mainframe downsizing platform," he added. "Now, 
CONVEYOR will be available on both OpenVMS and OSF/1 UNIX 
platforms."

     CONVEYOR for the OpenVMS platform consists of software tools 
that enable computer-aided execution of the migration steps, a 
methodology for the entire migration process, and global support 
from CONVEYOR service partners worldwide.

     Conversion provides a faster and more direct path than 
emulation to the native environments of target systems, at a 
fraction of the cost and resources usually needed for 
re-development. Through conversion, the basic functions of the 
source computer are replaced with basic functions available on the 
target Alpha computer. 

     As part of the Digital portfolio, CONVEYOR will provide safe, 
fast, economical application conversion in the mainframe downsizing 
process, while broadening market opportunities for the OpenVMS 
operating system running on the Alpha platform. 

     InfoSoft CONVEYOR permits the direct transition from monolithic 
mainframe solutions to the Alpha open system architecture. CONVEYOR 
supports a wide variety of popular mainframe operating systems, 
transaction processing systems, programming languages, screen 
management utilities, relational database management systems, and 
batch processing languages.

The OpenVMS on Alpha Environment

     Digital's Alpha platform is the ideal mainframe downsizing 
platform, based on performance, price/performance, choice of 
operating environment, scalability, and application availability.

     Industry-wide, Alpha 64-bit RISC-based servers are the clear 
performance leaders at every price level. Using industry-standard 
benchmarks, Alpha systems have set performance records in the 
overwhelming majority of categories, including on-line transaction 
processing (OLTP) against a relational database and single stream 
batch sorting. 

     The unique combination of OpenVMS business-critical 
functionality and Alpha power delivers major cost savings while 
actually increasing the performance, data integrity, and 
availability of many mainframe computing environments.

     The OpenVMS operating system is the only significant non-UNIX 
operating environment to be recognized and branded as open by the 
X/Open Consortium and the U.S. Government specification FIPS 151-2. 
The OpenVMS operating system has been awarded XPG4 base branding by 
X/Open -- ahead of many popular UNIX offerings, including IBM AIX 
and Sun Solaris operating systems.

     INFOSOFT GmbH is an international systems integrator in the 
Open Systems area, based in Dortmund, Germany.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions, from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage networking, software, and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
