           DIGITAL ENTERS CHINESE TEXT TERMINAL MARKET
 THROUGH JOINT DEVELOPMENT AGREEMENT WITH HUNAN COMPUTER FACTORY


BEIJING, PEOPLE'S REPUBLIC OF CHINA -- December 12, 1994 -- 
Digital Equipment Corporation and HuNan Computer Factory today 
announced that they have signed an agreement to supply text 
terminals for the Chinese market.  The agreement was signed today 
in HuNan Computer Factory's (HCF) Beijing office by HCF's CEO 
Yang De Quan and Vice President Zhicheng Sun, and by Brian 
Fitzgerald, Vice President of Video Products in Digital's 
Components and Peripherals Business Unit.

     Under the first phase of the agreement, Digital will design 
an Application Specific Integrated Circuit (ASIC) to be used in a 
future text terminal model to be manufactured by HCF.  This 
technology will enable HCF to meet its objective of lowering 
costs by employing the latest methodology in computer-related 
technology.  In addition to the ASIC, Digital will supply HCF 
with text terminal components, including monitors and keyboards.  
HCF will integrate its own logic board into the terminals, which 
it will manufacture and market under its own name in China.  This 
cooperative development effort will set the foundation for both 
companies to move forward in the planning process of providing 
localized products to the Asia Pacific market.

     This combination of the latest in hardware technology and 
world class quality will strengthen HCF's position as the leading 
text terminal manufacturer and supplier for the Chinese market.  

     The agreement will result in approximately $20 million of 
revenue for Digital.

     "We are pleased to announce that HuNan Computer Factory has 
chosen Digital's text terminals and we are excited to add them to 
our rapidly expanding list of technology partners," said 
Fitzgerald.  "Together, we will supply Chinese customers with 
cost-effective text terminals which are backed by both of our 
reputations for high quality and our proven customer service."

     "HuNan Computer Factory is excited to begin a business and 
technology partnership with Digital," said Quan.  "Digital's 
position as the recognized leader in video terminal technology 
will help us meet the needs of China's rapidly growing terminal 
market.  We expect this partnership to encompass more of 
Digital's industry-leading products in the future."

     Digital is the recognized industry leader in video 
technology and one of the world's largest suppliers of video text 
terminal products, with sales and service centers throughout the 
world, including Beijing, Shanghai and Shenzhen, China.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
