          DIGITAL EQUIPMENT EXHIBIT DRIVES HOME PERFORMANCE
                   LEADERSHIP OF ALPHA AND OpenVMS


         Texas Instruments, Liant Software & Magic Software
                 Port Their Applications to OpenVMS


ANAHEIM, California -- December 12, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation and its partners are demonstrating the unequaled power 
of Alpha and OpenVMS at the DECUS trade show being held this week at 
the Anaheim Convention Center in Anaheim, California.  Powerful new 
software applications from Texas Instruments, Reliability and Magic, 
and an industry-first non-Digital workstation running OpenVMS, 
highlight the OpenVMS exhibit.

     At Booth 464, Alpha microprocessors and the OpenVMS operating 
system are at the heart of the show's highest performing systems.  
Workstations and PCs running OpenVMS from Digital Equipment and 
Aspen Systems are demonstrating a variety of newly ported 
applications in the areas of database management and application
development.

Texas Instruments Make Available Composer by IEF* for OpenVMS

     The Texas Instruments (TI) software business announced today 
that Composer by IEF will be available for Digital Equipment's 
OpenVMS operating system on 64-bit Alpha-powered systems, beginning 
in the first quarter of 1995.  TI's Composer is a model-driven, 
integrated software application development solution for client/
server environments. Composer for IEF includes two specific software 
products that are available for the Alpha OpenVMS line:

     o 	The Implementation Toolset software runs on a computer 
        configured with the final target platform.  It ensures the 
        automation of the compilation, linking, and installation of 
        the Composer-developed applications

     o 	The Client/Server Encyclopedia provides a repository of 
        reuseable components for software application development 
        among workgroups in a client/server environment.

     "Digital's Alpha line offers high reliability, price/
performance systems required for today's growing companies, and TI 
provides the tools to develop client/server software required to 
meet the changing business needs," said Duncan McClain, director of 
marketing for the TI software division.  "With Composer available 
for the OpenVMS Alpha platform, customers will have the best 
solution available to enable them to develop and deploy client/ 
server applications in the distributed environments where maximum 
scalability and flexibility is required," McClain added.

Relativity, Inc. Demonstrates Relativity* for Alpha OpenVMS

     Relativity, Inc., a division of Liant Software, will also be 
demonstrating Relativity for DEC COBOL, a new developer application, 
running on Digital's Alpha and VAX OpenVMS systems.  Relativity is a 
revolutionary software tool that provides direct relational access 
to existing DEC COBOL data without the inefficiencies of gateways, 
data warehousing or replication.  Relativity is the latest in a
series of software tools to help developers integrate existing data 
and applications with new open client/server systems.

     "Digital's Alpha systems are an ideal platform for Relativity," 
said Bruce Flory, director of marketing for Relativity, Inc.  "The 
speed of Alpha technology, combined with the price/performance of 
these systems, their scalability from desktop to data center, and 
the robustness of OpenVMS Clusters provides the platform support 
developers need to integrate existing systems with client/server 
developments."

Magic Software Enterprises Also Chooses OpenVMS

     Magic Software Enterprises will be announcing and demonstrating 
their MAGIC rapid application development (RAD) system for Alpha 
systems running OpenVMS the first day of DECUS.  MAGIC's RAD 
capability comes from its unique visual programming methodology, 
through which developers describe applications in terms of their 
functionality and complete tables with details about data, event
control, users interface and other requirements.

     "By teaming with Digital, we can provide a complete systems 
solution to help MIS organizations integrate VAX, Alpha and other 
platforms," said David Wegman, chief operating officer for Magic.  
"Our partnership with Digital helps Magic develop a wider choice of 
options for corporate developers and VARs using Alpha systems -- or 
getting ready to do so.

Industry-First Agreement to Load OpenVMS on Aspen Workstations

     Aspen Systems, Inc. of Wheat Ridge, Colo. will also be debuting 
their Alpha-powered ALPINE* workstations running OpenVMS.  Digital 
and Aspen announced jointly today a licensing agreement to package 
the OpenVMS operating system on their high-performance line of 
workstations.  This represents the first commitment by a hardware 
vendor outside of Digital to load OpenVMS right on their Alpha systems.

     "The performance of the Alpha microprocessor allows us to 
create very powerful systems which will increase the OpenVMS systems 
presence in small-to-medium-sized enterprises (SME).  The rapidly 
expanding SME market demands the business critical functionality of 
OpenVMS," notes Steven Spring, CEO of Aspen Systems, Inc.  "In 
addition, we see great growth potential as more and more 
applications port to the OpenVMS operating system -- that adds up 
to a tremendous market opportunity for us."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
