            DIGITAL INTRODUCES STORAGEWORKS FDDI SERVERS;
        ADVANCED FUNCTION STORAGE FOR FDDI VAXCLUSTER SYSTEMS


     Alpha Technology and StorageWorks Provide High Performance,
      High Availability Storage Solutions Direct to the Network


ANAHEIM, California -- December 12, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced StorageWorks FDDI Servers, integrating 
industry-leading Alpha technology with StorageWorks modular design 
to meet the high performance storage requirements of all FDDI-based 
VAXcluster systems, unrestricted by conventional controllers.

     The StorageWorks FDDI Server family extends the StorageWorks 
line with highly available servers to meet the I/O needs of the 
smallest to the largest FDDI-based VAXcluster system.  These new 
storage servers support a wide range of StorageWorks magnetic and 
solid-state disks, tape, optical and loader devices, for configuring 
the exact FDDI storage solution to meet the demands of a broad range 
of applications.

     The StorageWorks FDDI Server family will be demonstrated at 
Fall DECUS here in booth 100 of Hall B in the Anaheim Convention 
Center.

     According to Bob Rennick, vice president and general manager of 
Digital's Storage Business Unit, "Our StorageWorks FDDI Servers 
complement the vastly broadened range of VAXcluster systems based on 
FDDI technology.

     The storage capacity, performance and data security 
requirements of such large scale systems are met by our new 
StorageWorks server family and they are flexible enough to grow in 
all these dimensions as technology and customer requirements 
evolve."

     Each StorageWorks FDDI Server is an independent VAXcluster 
member.  This means that multiple servers can be used in the same 
VAXcluster system, with OpenVMS operating system support for up to 
96 total nodes.

Initial offerings include:

     o  The Model HS111 StorageWorks FDDI Server, providing FDDI 
        access to up to 88GB of StorageWorks disk capacity, or other 
        storage devices

     o  The model HS121 StorageWorks FDDI Server, a fully redundant 
        server accessing up to 75GB of StorageWorks disk capacity, 
        or other storage devices.

