devices, for configuring the exact FDDI storage solution to meet any 
application's needs.

Customer Benefits:

    o  ONBOARD STORAGE MANAGEMENT - The full range of OpenVMS 
       storage management tools can be utilized to make both 
       StorageWorks FDDI Server models a truly "managed" storage 
       servers.  Because these utilities actually execute in the 
       Server Processor, they not only have minimal impact on 
       applications, but they significantly reduce I/O traffic on 
       the FDDI bus. 

    o  DATA SECURITY - As full VAXcluster members, the servers 
       provide a complete range of OpenVMS data security providing 
       block I/O services to hosts.  I/O services are restricted to 
       other members of the same VAXcluster system, low-level 
       (non-file) I/O is restricted to privileged users and provides 
       full protection of the OpenVMS file system for files 
       including access control by individual user if required.

    o  STORAGEWORKS MODULARITY - Since StorageWorks FDDI Servers 
       support a wide range of StorageWorks components (and can use 
       existing and future components), storage subsystems can be 
       custom configured to meet virtually any application need now 
       and can be easily upgraded when new technology is available.

    o  EASE OF USE - Each StorageWorks FDDI Server ships from the 
       factory with the OpenVMS operating system installed and
       preconfigured for use as a storage server in a VAXcluster
       system.  Installation consists of setting the server up for
       the specific storage device configuration (allocation 
       classes) and installing any optional storage management 
       software.

    o  DISTANCE - For customers requiring cluster connections beyond
       90 meters, the current CI limitation, FDDI network technology
       currently can be connected up to 40 kilometers.

    o  CONNECTIVITY - OpenVMS operating system supports up to 96 
       nodes in a single VMScluster versus 32 nodes in a CI cluster.

Competitive Comparison:

Digital's StorageWorks FDDI Server implementation provides a 
"managed storage" solution for the larger scale FDDI environment, 
extending the capabilities of a typical controller-to-network 
alternative.  Digital's FDDI storage server products are true 
servers in every sense of the word.

FUNCTIONALITY - The server approach allows data management to be 
off-loaded from a host or client.  Both basic operating system 
capabilities, such as OpenVMS Backup and extra-cost optional 
products, such as Polycenter Hierarchical Storage Manager (HSM) may 
be used with StorageWorks FDDI Servers.  Because these utilities 
actually execute in the server, they not only have minimal impact on 
applications, but they also significantly reduce I/O traffic on the 
bus.
                                                     
Channels Strategy:

The StorageWorks FDDI Server will be marketed and sold through both
direct sales and business partners.  Service will be available 
through normal service models.

