  ...Digital Semiconductor Widens Access, Development Support 
     for Alpha, PCI Chips...


                  DIGITAL ADDS 12 NEW DISTRIBUTORS
              TO WORLDWIDE SEMICONDUCTOR SALES CHANNEL


MAYNARD, Mass. -- December 13, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a major expansion of its worldwide distribution 
network for its Alpha and PCI semiconductor products with the naming 
of 12 new distributors in Europe, Asia, and Israel.

     "These 12 companies will add significantly to our international 
sales effort and strengthen our distribution channels as a merchant 
chip vendor," said Richard Riker, Digital Semiconductor's manager of 
Semiconductor Marketing and Sales.  "They will extend our global 
reach and boost access to Digital's Alpha microprocessors and PCI 
peripheral chips for system and component developers throughout the 
world."

     Eight of the new distributors are in Europe, three are in Asia, 
and one is in Israel.  They are:

     -- Memec Benelux b.v., Brussels, Belgium, and Eindhoven, Holland
     -- GB Topcomp Electronics, Copenhagen, Denmark
     -- Newtek, Paris (Rungis), France
     -- Metronik GmbH, Munich, Germany
     -- A. Scholz Electronics GmbH, Munich, Germany
     -- Bit Elektronikk A/S, Nesbru, Norway
     -- NC Nordcomp Sweden AB, Solna, Sweden
     -- Bytech Electronics Ltd, Basingstoke, UK
     -- Memec Asia-Pacific, Hong Kong, Korea, Taiwan
     -- Serial System Pte Ltd, Singapore
     -- Lumax International Corporation Ltd, Taipei, Taiwan
     -- Telsys Ltd, Tel Aviv, Israel

Chosen for Reputation, Expertise

     Each of the named distributors is among the largest in its 
respective geography.  Besides maintaining inventory as stocking 
distributors, they also provide design assistance and technical 
support for electronic products.  According to Riker, these 
companies were chosen because of their reputations as suppliers with 
customers, their technical capabilities, and their expertise in 
developing design-in solutions for semiconductor products.

     Applied Marketing and Technology (AM&T) Ltd., Digital 
Semiconductor's management company for European sales, was 
instrumental in effecting agreements with the seven companies in 
Europe.

     "AM&T has widely acknowledged expertise in establishing sales 
of U.S. semiconductor start-ups in Europe," said Riker.  "Digital 
Semiconductor is in the early phase of exploiting its significant 
merchant market potential.  AM&T brings established skills, 
relationships, and a wealth of European experience."

To Offer Full Line of Alpha, PCI Peripheral Chips

     Digital products to be offered through the distributor network 
are the complete family of Alpha RISC microprocessors, including the 
world's performance-leading Alpha 21164 chip and the recently 
announced Alpha 21066A microprocessor with integrated PCI, and 
Digital's line of PCI peripheral chips for graphics, networking, and 
PCI-to-PCI bridging applications.

     "As with our distributors in the U.S., Digital Semiconductor 
has committed engineering, marketing, and sales resources to its new 
distribution partnerships in Europe, Israel, and Asia," Riker said. 
"We are currently conducting training seminars covering Digital 
Semiconductor's products for our partners' sales representatives and 
field application engineers.  We are also assisting them in building 
inventory and developing support services for Digital products."

     Digital Semiconductor's distributors in North America, 
announced in December 1993, include Wyle Laboratories;  Hamilton 
Hallmark, a division of Avnet, Inc.;  and Pioneer-Standard 
Electronics and its affiliate, Pioneer Technologies Group.

     Digital Semiconductor, a Digital Equipment Corporation business 
headquartered in Hudson, Massachusetts, designs, manufactures and 
markets industry-leading semiconductor products including Alpha 
microprocessors and PCI-based peripheral chips.  Digital 
Semiconductor operates fabrication facilities in Hudson and South 
Queensferry, Scotland, and design centers in Hudson;  Palo Alto, 
California;  Austin, Texas;  and Jerusalem, Israel.  A new, 
$450-million, sub-half-micron semiconductor fabrication facility 
opened this year in Hudson.  Alpha microprocessors are also 
manufactured by Mitsubishi Electric Company under a second-source 
agreement.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
