               DIGITAL NAMES MILLERICK VICE PRESIDENT,
          FINANCE, FOR THE PERSONAL COMPUTER BUSINESS UNIT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- December 13, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that John J. Millerick has joined the company as 
vice president, Finance, for the Personal Computer Business Unit.

     Millerick has worldwide responsibility for all aspects of 
financial management for Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  
This includes financial control, accounting and management 
information as it relates to overall administration, manufacturing, 
engineering, and sales and marketing.  He reports to Bernhard Auer, 
vice president and general manager of Digital's Personal Computer 
Business Unit.

     "Digital is one of the fastest growing personal computer 
companies in the world," commented Bernhard Auer.  "As we move into 
the top tier it is imperative that we implement the financial 
procedures and controls necessary to succeed in this very 
competitive business.  We are very pleased that John Millerick has 
joined our team to help us manage this growth."

     Prior to joining Digital, Millerick was with Wang Laboratories 
where he held a number of senior positions in the U.S. and abroad, 
including corporate controller and acting CFO. Previously at Wang, 
he had finance responsibilities in support of several operational 
units including Product Development, Customer Service, Manufacturing, 
and Sales and Marketing.  Before Wang, Millerick was president of 
Publishers Design and Production Services, Inc.  He also held several 
management positions at Arthur Andersen & Co.

     Millerick holds a BA degree in mathematics from the College of 
the Holy Cross and an MBA from the Amos Tuck School of Business 
Administration at Dartmouth College.  He lives in Acton, 
Massachusetts.

