           MANUFACTURERS' REPRESENTATIVE HANNAH-HILL, INC.
              TO MARKET DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION'S
              ALPHA COMPUTERS IN ROCKY MOUNTAIN REGION


MAYNARD, Mass. -- December 19, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a new agreement with Hannah-Hill, Inc. -- a 
manufacturers representative serving OEM, government, scientific and 
industrial clients -- to market Digital's Alpha AXPvme line of 
64-bit RISC single board computer and real-time software to accounts 
throughout the central and southwestern U.S.

     With over 20 years of electronics sales experience, 
Hannah-Hill, Inc., a regional leader, specializes in marketing 
board-level products and computer systems for major electronic 
systems and components manufacturers.  Under the terms of the 
agreement, Hannah-Hill will market the following Digital products:  

     o 	The Alpha AXPvme line of 64-bit RISC PCI-based VME single 
       	board computers 

     o 	Alpha AXPpci33 PCI-based PC motherboards

     o 	The VxWorks for Alpha AXP real-time embedded software

     o 	The DEC OSF/1 UNIX operating system with real-time   
        extensions.

     "Hannah-Hill has created proactive marketing and support 
programs to keep in touch with their customers across a wide, 
sparsely-populated territory," said William Armitage, Vice President 
of Digital Equipment Corporation's Embedded and Real-time Products 
Business. "Because Hannah-Hill's field offices are electronically 
linked to the company's Denver headquarters, customers are ensured 
timely order processing, quotations, delivery information and technical 
support."

     "Digital Equipment wanted an Intermountain and Southwest 
partner that we could rely on to keep new customers happy," Armitage 
continued. "Hannah-Hill met all of our requirements."

     Ronald Hill, President of Hannah-Hill, Inc., was enthusiastic 
about adding Digital's industry-leading single board computer 
products and real-time software to his company's portfolio.  
"Digital is recognized by our OEM and industrial customers as a 
high-quality technology leader, dedicated to customer service.  This 
reputation, combined with the Digital's superior OEM support 
programs, will significantly enhance Hannah-Hill's overall 
offerings."

     According to industry analyst Warren Andrews, publisher of 
Embedded Computing Trends, "Digital is pursuing the right strategy 
with these nationwide channel building efforts.  In the VME and PCI 
bus arenas, manufacturers representatives with an established 
technical customer base can create rapid inroads to new accounts."

     With offices in Denver, Phoenix, Salt Lake City and 
Albuquerque, Hannah-Hill's market territory represents one-third of 
the continental U.S.  The company's staff of technically-trained 
sales engineers provide application support, product demonstrations 
and technical assistance to customers in eight states.

