           DIGITAL'S POLYCENTER PRODUCTS CLAIM TOP HONORS
             AT ENTERPRISE MANAGEMENT SUMMIT "SHOOT-OUT"


     Digital wins with POLYCENTER NetView, POLYCENTER Scheduler
                      and POLYCENTER AssetWORKS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- December 28, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
was honored with four top awards for its POLYCENTER network and 
system management products at the Enterprise Management Summit, held 
in late November in Santa Clara, Calif.  The honors were bestowed 
upon POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for auto-topology, POLYCENTER 
Scheduler for both production management and configuration 
management, and POLYCENTER AssetWORKS for software distribution. 

     Digital finished second in the overall competition by winning 
four out of the thirteen categories, ahead of competitors Hewlett-
Packard and Computer Associates, with two wins each, and Bull with 
one. IBM nudged Digital out of first place by winning five 
categories. 

     According to one of the judges, John Poitevin of US West 
Technologies, Digital had the "most sophisticated technical 
solutions."  The panel was particularly "impressed with the speed of 
discovery" in the auto-topology scenario; running on an Alpha 
workstation, POLYCENTER NetView blew by the rest of the competition.

     "This type of benchmarking proves the true value of our 
POLYCENTER management solutions," stated Nancy Strecker, vice 
president, Digital Software Products. "Digital has been delivering 
superior management solutions for years, and we are continuing to 
develop the technology that will be needed for the future.  We are 
pleased that the results of the Enterprise Management Summit confirm 
that our approach is paying dividends." 

     The production job scheduling competition was captured by 
POLYCENTER Scheduler with its simple graphical user interface.  This 
category required scheduling multiple jobs on multiple systems with 
interdependencies and priorities.  Judges were impressed by its ease 
of use. 

     POLYCENTER Scheduler also won the configuration category, 
where a new network setup was automatically loaded into a router.  
Scheduler was able to complete the reconfiguration at a 
predetermined time. 

     POLYCENTER AssetWORKS impressed judges with the top score in 
software distribution, compiling the highest average of any category 
in the competition, 4.5 on a scale of 5.  The combination of 
AssetWORKS and Microsoft's Systems Management Server (SMS) clearly 
demonstrated the power of the Windows NT platform. AssetWORKS 
extends the system inventory and software distribution capabilities 
of SMS beyond PCs to include multivendor UNIX and OpenVMS systems. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in managed 
open client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
